title: Payers › Process › Edit the workflow
route: /payers/summit?tab=process
intro: 'Edit workflow' opens a wide drawer with one card per step. Changes are held in the drawer and counted at the bottom; nothing reaches the payer's workflow until 'Save workflow' (next diagram). Conditions have their own diagram.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'Edit workflow'\non the workflow card"
overlay dr "Edit workflow drawer\nHow an authorization works with Summit.\nVersion 7 now, 8 when you save."
toast bn "'Steps run in order. A condition sends the case down\nanother path when it is true. Save asks for a reason\nand logs the old and new text.'"
screen sc "One card per step\nNumber, title box, step-type menu,\nup arrow, down arrow, bin"
process copy "Works on a copy of the steps\nThe saved workflow is untouched until Save"

group gE "On one step card"
  input i1 "Type the step title"
  input i2 "Pick the step type\nChecklist, File, Portal or Phone step"
  input i3 "Type 'What happens'"
  input i4 "Type 'Typical time'\nExample: 2 minutes"
  process ag "'Done by' agent chips are shown, not editable"
endgroup

group gM "Order and removal"
  click up "Click the up arrow\n'Move step 2 up'"
  click dn "Click the down arrow\n'Move step 2 down'"
  toast dis "Up is greyed out on step 1\nDown is greyed out on the last step"
  click rm "Click the bin\n'Remove step 2'"
  process rm2 "Step vanishes at once\nNo confirmation, numbers close up"
endgroup

click add "Click 'Add a step'"
process nw "Step added at the end\nTitle 'New step', Checklist step,\nblank text, '1 minute', no agents, no conditions"
click ac "Click 'Add a condition'\non a step"
goto gc "Continues in: Payers › Process › Add and edit conditions"

process cnt "Footer counts changes against the saved workflow\n'No changes yet' or '2 changes not saved yet'\nPutting a step back where it was removes its change"
click sv "Click 'Save workflow'"
goto gs "Continues in: Payers › Process › Save the workflow"
click cx "Click 'Cancel'"
click cesc "Press Escape, click the X\nor click the dimmed area\nEscape with a step menu open\ncloses only the menu"
endx x1 "Drawer closes\nEvery unsaved change is dropped\nNo 'are you sure'"

s1 --> dr --> bn --> sc --> copy
sc --> i1 & i2 & i3 & i4
i4 -.-> ag
sc --> up & dn & rm
up --> dis
dn --> dis
rm --> rm2
dr --> add --> nw
sc --> ac --> gc
i1 --> cnt
i2 --> cnt
i3 --> cnt
i4 --> cnt
up --> cnt
dn --> cnt
rm2 --> cnt
nw --> cnt
cnt --> sv --> gs
dr --> cx --> x1
dr --> cesc --> x1
